1
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,170
We learned one thing, C.H.E.E.S.E:

2
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:08,920
Cheerleaders and high explosives don't mix.

3
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,260
You can say that again, Mac.

4
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:16,010
I couldn't have done it alone. You're a genius.

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:21,350
Oh, yeah? Well, how come I can't get my VCR to stop blinking 12:00?

6
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:29,730
What did you guys think?

7
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:36,860
- Hey, the phone.     - I got it. I got it.

8
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:38,410
Hello.

9
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,370
- Hold on. Joey, it's your mom.     - It's Mommy.

10
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:41,910
- Aw...     - That's nice.

11
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,000
Ma, so what did you think?

12
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:46,120
Well...

13
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:48,920
...that was, um, okay.

14
00:00:49,170 --> 00:00:50,500
It wasn't the best.

15
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:53,210
That was one of the worst things ever...

16
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:56,970
...and not just on TV.

17
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:59,890
- What should we say?     - The lighting was okay.

18
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:03,220
You got lighting last time. Lighting is mine.

19
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:04,730
I have costumes.

20
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:06,390
That means I'm stuck with:

21
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:11,770
"So we were watching you in there, and you were sitting right here. Whoa."

22
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,940
- What about you?     - I don't know.

23
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,490
I can't lie to him again. Oh, no, I... No.

24
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:21,490
I'm just gonna press my breasts up against him.

25
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:25,080
- And say nothing?      - Uh-huh, yeah, that's right.

26
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:29,170
Wow, my folks really liked it.

27
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:30,920
What did you guys think?

28
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,090
It wasn't that good.

29
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:25,060
Do you think that your favorite animal says much about you?

30
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,100
You mean behind my back?

31
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:31,900
Oh, you'll never believe what happened to me today.

32
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:34,270
- I am sitting in my office...     - You guys!

33
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,190
Guess what my agent just said?

34
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,150
I'm in the middle of a story here.

35
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,740
Sorry, you finish.

36
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:42,870
I'm sitting in my office, and guess who walks in.

37
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,160
I'm gonna be on two TV shows.

38
00:02:45,410 --> 00:02:46,450
That's great.

39
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:49,370
- Joey.     - You weren't finished?

40
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:52,330
Yeah, "Guess who walks into my office" is my story.

41
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,000
Ralph Lauren walked into my office.

42
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:59,920
Uh, if you're starting another story, at least let me finish mine.

43
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:02,720
It's the same story.

44
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:05,760
Uh, wow, it's really long.

45
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:10,180
Ralph just came in to tell me that he's so happy with my work...

46
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,650
...that he wants me to be the new merchandising manager for Polo retail.

47
00:03:13,810 --> 00:03:14,860
Aw...

48
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,860
- Still get a discount on wedding gowns?     - Yeah.

49
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,190
I'm so happy for you.

50
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:22,910
These really are the days of our lives.

51
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:26,240
- What?     - Well, since you ask, ha, ha...

52
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:28,370
They want me back on Days of our Lives.

53
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:32,080
- I get a big pay raise!     - Oh, hey!

54
00:03:32,330 --> 00:03:34,830
I'll be playing Drake Ramoray's twin brother, Stryker.

55
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,540
Ooh...

56
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:38,210
I get to hire my own assistant.

57
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:43,510
Well... I got a head rush from standing up too fast.

58
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:51,140
You were at this job four years?

59
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:55,440
- That's right.     - This is all very impressive, Hilda.

60
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:59,360
Um, I just have one last question for you, uh...

61
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,440
How did I do? Was this okay?

62
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,990
- What?     - I've never interviewed anyone.

63
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,320
I've never had anyone work for me.

64
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,870
When I was a kid we had a maid, but this isn't the same.

65
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,330
No, dear, it's not.

66
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:15,420
And I know that.

67
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:19,250
Well, thank you so much for coming in.

68
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,510
- Nice to meet you.     - Good meeting you.

69
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,130
All right.

70
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:26,260
I'm a total pro.

71
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:30,010
- Hello.     - Wow. Huh, um...

72
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:34,520
Hi, yes, I'm sorry. The models are down the hall.

73
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:37,020
I'm here about the assistant job.

74
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,560
Really?

75
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,940
Okay, well, then, all right. Well, just have a seat there.

76
00:04:43,110 --> 00:04:44,740
Um, so what's...? What your name?

77
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:46,070
Tag Jones.

78
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,120
Uh-huh, go on.

79
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,290
That's it. That's my whole name.

80
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:53,580
That's your whole name. Of course.

81
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:56,540
Okay, let's just have a look-see here.

82
00:04:56,790 --> 00:05:00,500
I haven't worked in an office before. I don't have much experience...

83
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:04,840
What are you talking about? You got three years painting houses...

84
00:05:05,470 --> 00:05:09,010
...two whole summers at T.G.I. Friday's.

85
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,930
It's lame, I know.

86
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,020
But I'm a goal-oriented person, eager to learn...

87
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:16,180
Just hold on a second, please.

88
00:05:20,610 --> 00:05:23,860
It's for Human Resources. Everybody has to. Would you stand up?

89
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:34,240
Ha, ha, no, no, no.

90
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,590
- Hey.     - Shh, shh, shh.

91
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:54,060
- Anyway, I should go.     - Okay. Bye.

92
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:56,060
- Hey, sweetie.     - Hi, sweetie.

93
00:05:56,310 --> 00:05:58,350
What was with all the whispering?

94
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,810
I can't tell you. It's a secret.

95
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:04,820
Secret? Married people aren't supposed to have secrets.

96
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:07,690
We love and respect one another too much.

97
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,530
Aw...

98
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,450
But still, no, ha, ha.

99
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:15,740
We should tell each other everything. I don't have secrets from you.

100
00:06:15,950 --> 00:06:20,460
Really? So tell me what happened to Ross, junior year at Disneyland.

101
00:06:20,710 --> 00:06:21,830
No, I can't do that.

102
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:25,170
I'll tell you what Phoebe said.

103
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,010
- Okay.     - Okay.

104
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:29,590
So, ahem, Ross and I are going to Disneyland.

105
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,010
We stop at this restaurant for tacos.

106
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:36,890
When I say restaurant, I mean a guy, a hibachi, and the trunk of his car.

107
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,560
So Ross has about ten tacos.

108
00:06:39,810 --> 00:06:44,360
Anyway, we're on Space Mountain and Ross starts to feel a little iffy.

109
00:06:44,610 --> 00:06:46,190
Oh, my God. He threw up?

110
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:49,400
No, he visited a town a little south of throw up.

111
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,030
Oh, my God!

112
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,410
What was Phoebe's secret?

113
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:57,910
Um, Nancy Thompson, from Phoebe's old massage place, is getting fired.

114
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,160
Oh.

115
00:07:02,670 --> 00:07:05,750
That's it? I gave up my Disneyland story for that?

116
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,920
Hm, that's right. You lose, sucker!

117
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,880
Please still marry me.

118
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,770
You have an assistant, right?

119
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:20,060
Did she call?

120
00:07:20,230 --> 00:07:24,100
You told her I was sick, right? Always tell her I am sick.

121
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:27,690
I don't know. How do you decide who to hire?

122
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:29,610
I have it down to two people.

123
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,900
One has great references and a lot of experience.

124
00:07:33,110 --> 00:07:35,530
- And then, there's this guy.     - What about him?

125
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:38,410
I love him.

126
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:42,290
He's so pretty, I want to cry.

127
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,870
I don't know what to do.

128
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:47,710
Come on, you know what to do. You hire the first one.

129
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:52,590
Don't hire assistants because they're cute. Do it because they're qualified.

130
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:54,590
Uh-huh.

131
00:07:56,010 --> 00:08:00,350
I hear you. You make a lot of sense. Can I just say one more thing?

132
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,810
Look how pretty.

133
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:04,940
Let me see.

134
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,940
Oh, my God.

135
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,480
Oh. But, no.

136
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,950
No. You can't... You can't hire him because it's not professional.

137
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:17,740
Um, this is for me, yes?

138
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:21,700
Okay, you're right. I'll hire Hilda tomorrow.

139
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:24,710
Dumb, old, perfect-for-the-job Hilda.

140
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:26,540
Let me see.

141
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:30,460
Wo-ha-ow!

142
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:32,760
Don't show this to Monica.

143
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,380
And don't tell her about the "Wo-ha-ow!"

144
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,500

145
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:44,060
- Ha, ha, hey, Joey.     - Hey, Terry.

146
00:08:44,310 --> 00:08:46,520
- Nice to see you again.     - Been a while.

147
00:08:46,730 --> 00:08:49,560
Funny, these halls look smaller than they used to.

148
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:52,150
It's a different building.

149
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,440
So...

150
00:08:54,950 --> 00:08:57,200
...Stryker Ramoray, huh?

151
00:08:57,450 --> 00:08:59,700
- When do I start?     - How about right now?

152
00:08:59,950 --> 00:09:01,330
Okay.

153
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:04,040
Here are the audition scenes.

154
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:10,210
I thought you were offering me the part.

155
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:11,550
Why?

156
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:14,170
I was Doctor Drake Ramoray, Stryker's twin brother.

157
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:18,050
Who looks more like me than me, right?

158
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:21,430
Everybody has to audition. Ha, ha.

159
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:26,140
You know, Terry, I don't really need to do this.

160
00:09:26,350 --> 00:09:29,060
I got my own cable TV series...

161
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,520
...with a robot.

162
00:09:32,650 --> 00:09:35,440
I'm sorry, Joey. That's the way it is.

163
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,610
Well...

164
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:40,780
...I guess you think you're pretty special, huh?

165
00:09:41,030 --> 00:09:44,490
Sitting up here in your fancy, small-halled building...

166
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,580
...making stars jump through hoops for you, huh?

167
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:50,330
Well, you know what?

168
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:55,010
This is one star whose hoop...

169
00:09:55,260 --> 00:09:57,420
This is the star the hoop... This hoop...

170
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,630
I was Doctor Drake Ramoray!

171
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:09,850
Hi, Tag. What are you doing here?

172
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:13,520
I came to thank you for not laughing in my face yesterday.

173
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:17,190
I noticed there were no plants so I brought you your first.

174
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,740
There is a plant in your office.

175
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:21,950
Kind of.

176
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:23,700
Right.

177
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:27,040
So I guess I shouldn't put "good at noticing stuff" on my résumé.

178
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,250
Oh...

179
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,620
- Thank you.     - Anyway...

180
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:32,920
...I'm guessing you hired somebody.

181
00:10:33,590 --> 00:10:34,790
Well...

182
00:10:35,170 --> 00:10:36,420
Gotcha.

183
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,920
Thanks again for meeting with me.

184
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,050
But I hired you.

185
00:10:44,010 --> 00:10:46,010
- What?     - Yeah, you got the job.

186
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,220
- You're my new assistant.     - I am?

187
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:49,890
Yeah.

188
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:54,360
- I can't believe it.     - Ha, ha, me either.

189
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,440
First, I need you to go downstairs...

190
00:10:58,690 --> 00:11:01,450
...find a woman named Hilda, and tell her to go home.

191
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:08,450
- Hey.     - Hey, good, you're home.

192
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,960
Always nicer to hear than, "Oh, crap, you again."

193
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:15,880
Hey, sweetie, I made you a surprise.

194
00:11:16,130 --> 00:11:17,960
- Oh, yeah?     - Yeah, tacos.

195
00:11:18,170 --> 00:11:21,170
Ever since that story, I've had such a craving.

196
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,300
Did you not understand the story?

197
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,220
- Hey.     - Hey, what's up?

198
00:11:29,390 --> 00:11:32,810
Ah, nothing. Just figuring out what to do for dinner.

199
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,610
Hey, ooh, what's that? Dinner stuff?

200
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,820
- You making dinner?     - No.

201
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,360
Shh!

202
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:45,370
What's over there? Tacos?

203
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:46,700
No. No.

204
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:49,870
They're just, uh... They're...

205
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,330
They're ground beef smileys.

206
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:55,630
Uh, those are tacos.

207
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,380
Excuse me, Mr. Mexico.

208
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:02,130
Either way, I'll pass. Still can't eat those.

209
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,090
Ha, ha.

210
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:12,060
What's so funny?

211
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,520
I'm not laughing.

212
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,950
You told her!

213
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,540
Nancy Thompson's getting fired.

214
00:12:36,710 --> 00:12:40,750
Okay, okay. I had food poisoning. It's not like I chose to do it!

215
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:44,880
It's not like I said, "What would make this ride more fun?"

216
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:49,680
Right. You're right, I'm sorry. I shouldn't be laughing.

217
00:12:49,930 --> 00:12:52,310
I should be laying down papers for you.

218
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:58,230
- How could you?     - I had to. We're getting married.

219
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:00,940
Married couples can't keep secrets.

220
00:13:01,150 --> 00:13:04,070
I... I guess Monica should know about Atlantic City.

221
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,950
Du... ude!

222
00:13:06,990 --> 00:13:09,910
- What happened?     - Chandler and I are in a bar...

223
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:12,540
Did you not hear me say, "Du... ude"?

224
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:16,710
And this girl is making eyes at Chandler.

225
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:21,710
So he goes over to her and, uh, after a minute or two, I see them kissing.

226
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:26,420
You're thinking he's not the type to go to bars and make out with girls.

227
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,680
And you're right. He's not the type...

228
00:13:28,930 --> 00:13:33,060
...to go to bars and make out with "girls."

229
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,770
You kissed a guy?

230
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,150
Oh, my God!

231
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:44,570
In my defense, it was dark and he was a very pretty guy.

232
00:13:46,490 --> 00:13:48,150
Oh, Mon, I laughed so hard...

233
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:52,530
Ho-ho, so hard we had to throw out your underwear again?

234
00:13:54,410 --> 00:13:56,620
Whatever, dude. You kissed a guy.

235
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,800
- Hi.     - Hey.

236
00:14:04,050 --> 00:14:05,760
How's Hilda working out?

237
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:11,390
Oh, my new assistant is working out. Yes.

238
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,220
She happy she got the job?

239
00:14:13,430 --> 00:14:18,940
My new assistant is very happy that I hired my new assistant.

240
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:22,360
Hello.

241
00:14:22,610 --> 00:14:24,940
Oh, hey! Can you hang on a second?

242
00:14:25,150 --> 00:14:27,240
It's the producers at Mac and C.H.E.E.S. E...

243
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,320
...if you'll excuse me for a minute.

244
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:35,490
Hey, funny you should call. I was just looking over next week's script.

245
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,000
Canceled?

246
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,460
Like, they're taking it off the air? Oh.

247
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,920
All right, I'll see you Monday.

248
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,720
We're not even shooting them anymore!

249
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,970
All right. Bye.

250
00:14:53,220 --> 00:14:54,970
They canceled Mac and C.H.E.E.S.E.

251
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,930
- Oh, sorry.      - Oh, sorry, Joey.

252
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:59,930
Why would they do that? It was a good show, right?

253
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,740
You want to tell secrets? Okay, in college...

254
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:17,120
...Ross used to wear leg warmers.

255
00:15:18,950 --> 00:15:24,500
All right, Chandler entered a Vanilla Ice look-alike contest and won.

256
00:15:26,250 --> 00:15:28,460
Ross came in fourth and cried!

257
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:30,470
Oh, my God!

258
00:15:31,260 --> 00:15:33,720
Oh, is that funny? You find that funny?

259
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:36,800
Maybe Chandler should know your secrets too.

260
00:15:36,970 --> 00:15:39,270
Ha, ha. Oh, I... I already told him everything.

261
00:15:39,430 --> 00:15:41,100
You shush!

262
00:15:42,060 --> 00:15:44,350
Once, she was sent to bed without dinner...

263
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:47,570
...so she ate the macaroni off a jewelry box she'd made.

264
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:54,070
Ross stayed home every Saturday night to watch Golden Girls.

265
00:15:56,530 --> 00:15:59,160
Monica couldn't tell time until she was 13.

266
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:03,500
It's hard for some people!

267
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:05,920
Of course it is.

268
00:16:06,130 --> 00:16:08,130
Wow.

269
00:16:08,590 --> 00:16:11,670
- Chandler wore my underwear to work!     -  Hey!

270
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:16,470
Oh, I'm sorry, I couldn't think of any more for Ross.

271
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:18,470
In college, Chandler got drunk...

272
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,720
...and slept with the lady who cleaned our dorm.

273
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:23,560
That was you.

274
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,690
Whatever, dude. You kissed a guy.

275
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,490
How could this happen to me?

276
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:38,450
Yesterday, I had two TV shows. Today, I got nothing.

277
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:41,540
Wait a minute, what happened to Days ofour Lives?

278
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:44,870
Uh, well, they might be a little mad at me over there.

279
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:46,540
What happened?

280
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:51,960
Well, maybe I got a little upset, and maybe I told them where they could go.

281
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:54,670
Joey, why would you do that?

282
00:16:54,930 --> 00:16:57,390
Because! They wanted me to audition.

283
00:16:57,590 --> 00:17:01,010
You, an actor? That's madness!

284
00:17:08,480 --> 00:17:10,310
Rachel Green's office.

285
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:13,860
Tag.

286
00:17:14,110 --> 00:17:15,570
Hi, who was that?

287
00:17:15,950 --> 00:17:19,070
Nobody. I was just practicing.

288
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:20,530
Really?

289
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:29,080
- Hi.     - Hi, Rachel Green's office.

290
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,800
- You must be Hilda.     - Ahem.

291
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,050
He's Tag. This is Phoebe.

292
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:38,180
- Phoebe, can I see you for a sec?     - Mm-hm.

293
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:39,510
- Phoebe.     - Mm-hm.

294
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:41,850
- Great name.     - You like that?

295
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:44,720
- You should hear my phone number.     - Okay.

296
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:53,270
So you hired yourself a little treat, did you?

297
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,650
I know how it looks, but I am telling you...

298
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:59,410
You can't get involved with your assistant.

299
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:04,370
I know that, and I know hiring him was not the smartest thing I've ever done.

300
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:07,370
But, from now on, I swear this is strictly professional.

301
00:18:08,750 --> 00:18:10,040
- Yes.     - Hey, Rachel.

302
00:18:10,210 --> 00:18:11,250
Hi.

303
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:14,050
Cute assistant. What's his story?

304
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:16,550
- Is he...?     - Gay? Yeah.

305
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:24,600
Hey, Terry.

306
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:26,100
Joey Tribbiani.

307
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:30,020
Surprised your big head could fit through our small halls.

308
00:18:31,150 --> 00:18:33,360
- I gotta go, Joey.     - Wait, Terry! Look, uh...

309
00:18:33,610 --> 00:18:35,530
I'm really sorry about before.

310
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:38,990
I was an idiot, thinking I'm too big to audition for you.

311
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:41,450
- Give me another chance.     - I can't.

312
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:43,490
Wait, Terry, please!

313
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:46,700
Look, I just lost my other job, okay?

314
00:18:46,950 --> 00:18:50,120
You have no idea how much I need this.

315
00:18:50,370 --> 00:18:51,870
Please, help me out.

316
00:18:52,250 --> 00:18:54,170
For old times' sake.

317
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:58,800
This guy's been in a coma for five years. It's hopeless.

318
00:18:59,050 --> 00:19:02,050
It's not. Dr. Stryker Ramoray is a miracle worker.

319
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,340
Here he comes.

320
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:05,640
Good morning.

321
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:16,480
Drake, it's your brother, Stryker. Can you hear me?

322
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:18,030
And cut.

323
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,110
I'm back, baby!

324
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:37,670
You know, in my defense, um...

325
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:41,510
...there was no glitter on the macaroni and very little glue.

326
00:19:41,970 --> 00:19:45,510
And in my defense, the cleaning lady came on to me.

327
00:19:46,970 --> 00:19:49,970
- Do you have trouble telling time now?     - No.

328
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,940
- Quick, what time is it?     - I don't know. Time to kiss a guy?

329
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,730
What are you laughing at, Pampers?

330
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:04,280
You know when I said married people...

331
00:20:04,530 --> 00:20:07,370
...should share everything and not have any secrets?

332
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:10,450
- Yeah?     - That was stupid. Let's not do that.

333
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:11,700
Oh.

334
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,160
Absolutely.

335
00:20:13,330 --> 00:20:17,460
We should keep the stuff we told each other secret from everyone else.

336
00:20:17,710 --> 00:20:19,550
Yeah, definitely.

337
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,010
Okay, ha, ha.

338
00:20:22,170 --> 00:20:24,680
If you'll excuse me, I'm gonna hang out with people...

339
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:27,350
...who don't know the Space Mountain story.

340
00:20:27,930 --> 00:20:31,850
- Then I'd steer clear of Phoebe.     - Man!

341
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:37,810
Not that you would, but I wouldn't hang out with the guys at my office.

342
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:49,700
Hi.

343
00:20:51,950 --> 00:20:54,410
- Do you have a minute?     - Sure. What's up?

344
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:58,500
I got asked out twice today while I was at lunch...

345
00:20:58,750 --> 00:21:00,460
...by guys.

346
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:03,970
- Really?     - Yeah.

347
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:06,590
Did you tell someone that I was gay?

348
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:10,140
Oh, did you not want people to know that?

349
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:16,190
I'm not gay. I especially wouldn't want you to think I was gay.

350
00:21:16,690 --> 00:21:18,270
Why is that?

351
00:21:20,190 --> 00:21:23,690
- I don't think I should say.     - Oh, you can say.

352
00:21:25,530 --> 00:21:29,200
Come on, I don't want you to feel like you can't tell me things.

353
00:21:31,910 --> 00:21:33,080
- Okay.     - Okay.

354
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:35,910
- Well...     - Yeah.

355
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:38,670
...I'd love to ask out your friend Phoebe.

356
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:43,460
Yeah, she's gay.

